codex
A stronger audit found the important Track B boundary: a full-constraint packed-bitset greedy solver with legal one-vertex repair does solve these instances, while the intentionally cheap sampled greedy does not. I’ve moved that successful domain-standard method into `reference_algorithm`, retained four failing no-tool attacks, and kept the affine scan as a separately disclosed complete solver for the generated distribution. The measured gap is now against the right baseline, not an artificially weak one.
