codex
The reliability sweep passed on 40 additional shipping seeds, including deterministic regeneration, exact witness verification, compact recovery under the 300-operation cap, JSON round-trip, parser garbage rejection, and hint isolation. The module and report artifacts compile and parse cleanly. The only unmet release condition is external: there are zero valid oracle attempts because the configured OpenRouter key is over its total limit.
The generator and all local deliverables are complete and verified. The bare and G9 hardening runs were executed but could not obtain any valid oracle attempt because OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 on every redraw; this external limitation is preserved in the script-owned transcripts and documented in the README.
  ✓ Read the full paper and triage G/H/V, including mechanical versus compact cost
  ✓ Inspect repository harnesses and available exact-arithmetic helpers
  ✓ Design and implement the generator or write a fully evidenced rejection
  ✓ Run self-tests, adversary measurements, and canonical-key checks
  ✓ Run the required hardening and G9 oracle arms if a family survives
  ✓ Write final machine-readable reports and README, then verify deliverables
